  "live_records": {
    "q-158309": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158309",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Compute $P(X\\le 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{24}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{24}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}[(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3)-(\\frac{1}{3}+1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}(12-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot \\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
