    "q-158310": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158310",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Compute $P(X>-3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2},\\, & -6\\le x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>-3) & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{216}{x}^{3}]}_{-3}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{216}[(0)^{3}-(-3)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{216} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
