    "q-158461": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158461",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Compute $P(X\\le 0)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}(3{x}^{2}+2x+1),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 0) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{20}(3{x}^{2}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}3{x}^{2}+2x+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{[{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}([{0}^{3}+{0}^{2}+0]-[(-2)^{3}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(0-[-8+4-2]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
